link: SANS ISC, fake Homebrew page (Binance's reference) | https://isc.sans.edu/diary/32942
notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites, in two slides. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Binance's November 3 initial findings carry the stage-by-stage account. Its two October 30 updates carry the earlier account and the statement that no evidence of leaked private keys had been found. TRM, Elliptic and Chainalysis read the chain and give their own figures and times. Trail of Bits draws general lessons for signing systems.

The SANS Internet Storm Center diary is the page Binance links as its reference for a tampered Homebrew installation. It does not mention Binance.

